Realistic BWR — licensing
=========================

This project is open source under a two-module split. The boundary is the same
one the architecture already draws: physics that has nothing to do with
Minecraft, versus the mod that embeds it.

  core/  — MIT.        See core/LICENSE
  mod/   — MPL-2.0.    See mod/LICENSE

Why the split
-------------

core/ is a pure-Java boiling water reactor model with zero Minecraft imports.
It is independently useful outside this mod, so MIT keeps it maximally
reusable — anyone can take the reactor physics for a simulator, a teaching
tool, or another game.

mod/ is the NeoForge integration. MPL-2.0 is file-level copyleft: improvements
to these files come back, but the licence does not reach players' Lua scripts
or other mods sharing a pack. That matters because stronger copyleft creates
real friction in modpack distribution. It is also what CC:Tweaked chose for its
own newer code.

Player-written code
-------------------

This mod deliberately ships no control logic. Every scram channel, setpoint,
protection scheme, and emergency-system actuation sequence is written by the
player in CC:Tweaked Lua.

Lua programs written by players are the players' own work. They are not
derivative works of this mod, and neither licence above applies to them.
Players own what they write, without condition.

Third-party dependencies
------------------------

CC:Tweaked — compile-time only, and deliberately never bundled. Parts of its
API remain under LicenseRef-CCPL, which permits redistribution only
"unmodified and in full"; IPeripheral.java still carries that header. This
project therefore depends on it via compileOnly and players install
CC:Tweaked themselves. Do not vendor, shade, or copy CC:Tweaked source into
this tree.

Mekanism — MIT. A hard runtime dependency, used for the fuel-crafting and
steam-turbine boundaries.

NeoForge — LGPL-2.1. Linking against it does not affect this project's
licensing.

Reference data
--------------

Plant constants in REFERENCE-DATA.md are drawn from the U.S. Nuclear
Regulatory Commission's Boiling Water Reactor Systems Manual, BWR/6 Design
(ADAMS accession ML20090J537), a public United States Government document.
Physical facts — pressures, flow rates, geometry, delayed neutron data — are
not subject to copyright. The source document itself is deliberately not
committed to this repository; it is cited by accession number so anyone can
retrieve it from the NRC directly.
